From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:48:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 073/342] Tracker: breadcrumb buttons above the Navigator's
 location field

jrash's tracker-breadcrumbs change, applied as is: IRIX-style path buttons, one per path component and lined up with its
text in the location field. A click goes to that folder and selects the
one you came from; Option-click opens it in a new window; the jumps are
part of the Back/Forward history; a press released outside does nothing;
the tool tip shows the full path; the buttons follow the text when a long
path scrolls. BreadcrumbBar.cpp/.h are new; Navigator stacks the bar on
the location field and handles its clicks.

The Navigator only shows with Tracker preferences -> Windows -> Single
window navigation and Show navigator.

Tested on the ODROID-C2 with the change's GUI test (17 checks, real mouse
and key events; the port's copy in tools/tracker-breadcrumbs): all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
